    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Major clinical and pathological features of EBV-positive hydroa vacciniforme lymphoproliferative disorder (HV-LPD)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Leticia Quintanilla-Martinez",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"margin-left: -.5pt; border-collapse: collapse; \" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" \">\r\n<td style=\"width: 57.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>HV-LPD</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical presentation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical behaviour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Morphology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunophenotype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Molecular findings</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 60.85pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 57.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Classic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vesicles and papules in sun-exposed areas</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Indolent, self-limited disease</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Remission with photoprotection in the majority of cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Epidermal vesicles with superficial perivascular and periappendiceal infiltrates</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cytotoxic CD4+ or CD8+ T&nbsp;cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.85pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Polyclonal&nbsp;/ rare monoclonal TR genes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBER+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 104.9pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 57.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Systemic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vesiculopapular and ulcerative lesions, facial oedema in sun-exposed and non&ndash;sun-exposed areas</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Fever</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often lymphadenopathy and hepatosplenomegaly</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Remissions and recurrences</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Progression to leukaemia/lymphoma or HLH</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High EBV DNA load in blood</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Response to treatment with immunomodulators or HSCT</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoid infiltrate with variable degrees of atypia in superficial and deep dermis including the subcutaneous tissue</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mainly cytotoxic CD8+ cells, rarely CD4+ or NK cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 104.9pt;\" width=\"171\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monoclonal TR genes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBER+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBER, EBV-encoded small RNA; HLH, haemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis; HSCT, haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]